Package: LeeDiD
Title: Bounds on Intensive Margin Treatment Effects in Panel Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Javier", "Viviens", , "javier.viviens@eui.eu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements the identification and estimation strategy of
    Viviens (2026) for the intensive margin treatment effect in panel data
    settings. Adapts the Horowitz-Manski-Lee bounds to the
    Changes-in-Changes framework to partially identify the average and
    quantile treatment effect on the treated among 'Always Observed' units,
    leveraging multiple sources of sample selection jointly to relax the
    monotonicity assumption behind the original bounds. Provides point
    estimates, bootstrap standard errors, and Imbens-Manski confidence
    intervals for the resulting identified sets.
